# What a `vercel deploy` from the repository root must NOT upload.
#
# The docs project's Root Directory is `docs`, but the build needs the whole
# tree: `docs/scripts/sync-generated.mjs` copies the diagrams from `assets/` at
# the repository root, because both READMEs reference them from there. So the
# upload is the repo, not just `docs/` — which makes this file the only thing
# standing between a local-only directory and a deployment.
#
# `docs/internal/` is the reason this file exists. It is the engineering journal:
# gitignored, deliberately absent from the remote, and present on every machine
# that has ever run this project. A CLI deploy uploads the working tree rather
# than a git clone, so without this line it would ride along into a deployment
# whose source is one API call away from anyone holding a token.
docs/internal/

# Build output and caches. Regenerated by the build; uploading them wastes the
# upload and risks handing Turbopack a cache that names another machine's paths.
node_modules/
dist/
.next/
.source/
docs/out/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Local run artifacts: work directories can be hundreds of megabytes.
work/
runs/

# Never. `.env.example` is generated and committed; a real `.env` is not.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.DS_Store
*.log
